{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787313692401645001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bemused-painted-worm","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"64387f00cbdd0692b056269156abbb17442c6d583bc0b67cb01866f43e592399","event_uuid":"219d37f8-45a8-434d-ae4c-d3ae32e7710b","position":{"commit_sha":"c7f732419be473783e9b8f9659e29ca3f5b66224","position":"1787309327931304001-219d37f8-45a8-434d-ae4c-d3ae32e7710b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2ff0b669c38d6567e55f35b80001c6f9023764bb219b00f5f5589a70d6ac4d48","event_uuid":"a95488a3-08e9-4bea-97ec-8cdfc764cffd","position":{"commit_sha":"79bd12c508e38fe4ae4c19ea208e2f1d3fb85a34","position":"1787309340725690001-a95488a3-08e9-4bea-97ec-8cdfc764cffd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d75797f558b00c7de657be0c7ad3c023f3259ed7ac487bb83dd939be2ba8c891","event_uuid":"fb42076f-8eea-4613-ad2b-4d6439b9f458","position":{"commit_sha":"774bfd78a8e470fe735d78121e2e9cbb5cc35fa4","position":"1787309348235056001-fb42076f-8eea-4613-ad2b-4d6439b9f458"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787309327931304001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a95488a3-08e9-4bea-97ec-8cdfc764cffd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"93a9-66cf-e681-4f49"}],"description":"## Context\n\nFound by the Step-7 parity sweep of bug `intangible-ladyish-vicuna` (`93a9-66cf-e681-4f49`),\nwhich restored the compaction trigger's sidecars to the canonical store.\n\n`doctor_locks.scan_locks` (`src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py:321-360`) canonicalises the\ntracker and then reports four legs — `tickets-write-fcntl`, `tickets-write-mkdir`, `hlc`,\n`enrich-drain` (`doctor_locks.py:90-93`). There is NO leg for `compact-worker.lock`, even\nthough it is a stamped advisory lock in the same `.rebar/`, arbitrated by the same\n`lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale` decision table as the drain lock next to it.\n\nConsequence: a compaction worker that dies between acquire and release leaves a stamped lock\nthat `rebar doctor` cannot see, so the one diagnostic built to answer \"who holds what\" is\nsilent about the lock most likely to be held by a detached background process. (The lock IS\nself-healing via the shared staleness table, so this is observability, not correctness.)\n\nNote: the `intangible-ladyish-vicuna` description asserted that \"`rebar doctor` describes the\ncanonical `compact-worker.lock`\". It does not — that assumption was checked and disproved\nduring the debug session, which is what surfaced this gap.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd a `compact-worker` leg to `scan_locks` alongside `enrich-drain`, reusing the existing\nstamped-file report helper. Deliberately NOT done inside the bug fix: adding a doctor leg is\nnew capability, and that fix was held to restoration only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar doctor` reports a `compact-worker` lock leg, on the canonical store, with the\n      same held-for / staleness / holder detail the `enrich-drain` leg carries.\n- [ ] A test covers a held compact-worker lock appearing in the census and a free store not\n      reporting a spurious holder.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, complexity ratchet and the unit sweep green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py","reason":"add the compact-worker lock leg to the census"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_locks.py","reason":"cover the new leg held and free"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8a0d-96ca-a60e-4da6","ticket_type":"task","title":"doctor's lock census has no compact-worker leg","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["219d37f8-45a8-434d-ae4c-d3ae32e7710b","a95488a3-08e9-4bea-97ec-8cdfc764cffd","fb42076f-8eea-4613-ad2b-4d6439b9f458"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787313692401645001,"uuid":"fead0b3f-1f2f-4d59-86b3-132802411ad8"}